          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A delta lens (or d-lens) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            with additional structure specifying a suitable choice of lifts. Delta lenses can be understood in a number of ways:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A morphism between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
                which is both
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofunctor"} cofunctor
            %li
              %p
                A generalization of split
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+fibration"} Grothendieck opfibrations
                where the chosen lifts need not be
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+morphism"} opcartesian morphisms
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertical+categorification"} categorification
                of classical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lens+%28in+computer+science%29"} lenses
                between
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            A
            %strong delta lens
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f, \varphi) : A \to B
            from a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            consists of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor"} functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : A \to B
            together with a
            %em lifting operation
            sending each pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo :
                  %mi f
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a \in A, u : f a \to b \in B)
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi φ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi u
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(a, u) : a \to a'
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo =
                    %mi cod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi φ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi u
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' = cod(\varphi(a, u))
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                defines a choice of lifts:
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi u
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \varphi(a, u) = u
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                preserves identity morphisms:
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mrow
                            %mi f
                            %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mn 1
                          %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(a, 1_{f a}) = 1_{a}
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi
                preserves composition:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi v
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo ,
                      %mi u
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \varphi(a, v \circ u) = \varphi(a', v) \circ \varphi(a, u)
                where
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %mi cod
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi a
                        %mo ,
                        %mi u
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' = cod(\varphi(a, u))
          %div{:style => "text-align: center"}
